fortunately that heartbreaking story  isn't the only tragedy to come out of  the windy city this weekend as the  carnage continues on the streets of  chicago between friday and sunday there  were 54 shooting incidents wounding 86  and killing 13 people now our outraged  residents are asking where is the mayor  lori lightfoot as the city spires out of  control  under her watch brittany benson knows  the true cost of lifeless failure as her  15-year-old son demarion was gunned down  on the city streets last month and  another example of the senseless  violence  brittany benson joins me now along with  violence interrupter executive director  t.o hardiman uh brittany can you tell me  the story of your son demarion when you  got that phone call  what did you do  well what happened was i talked to  demaryon about 5 53.  he had asked me what i was doing and i  told him i was cooking and he was like  oh yeah oh yeah i'm coming home i'm like  well you know come home cause you know  we got to take care of some important  business  he was like  i ma i love you mom  and that was the last time i spoke with  him so  it had to be like around like 6 11. my  mom was calling me back to back  so i didn't pick up i'm like maybe she  didn't want nothing at that moment i  wasn't thinking and so  my sister-in-law called me she was like  tell me this not true me  i'm like what did you what are you  talking about so  my sister called me she was like she was  crying she was like where you at mimi  astrological hospital so you know i  guess the australia hospital and i knew  something was wrong because at that  moment  it felt like  my stomach  was caving in and they feel like i had  to regurgitate it it was weird and it  just  it felt awkward like i knew something  was wrong and then  30 minutes later they told me he was  deceased  brittany you said that he was your eyes  yes i was born with um a condition  called congenital glaucoma  and he was everything  and he was his mama's eyes um i want to  go to uto you have been on the streets  for a while talking with the community  trying to bring  uh some type of justice in that city  what do you think it would take right  now to end the violence in chicago  well first i just want to send my  condolences out to officer uh french and  her family and also with brittany what i  plan to do here is assign five of my  staff to brittany 24 hours a day to help  her you know take her to the store  because she lost her son her son serves  served as another set of eyes for her so  i plan to allow some of my staff to take  her to the growth store and help her  when she runs errands number one and uh  number two i just want to say this what  it what it will take to really stop the  gun violence in chicago we need to  pretty much assemble a big unit of  african-american men that are really  concerned about these young guys out  here and we need to swarm the community  in big big numbers and actually bring  them guys to the table of peace and try  to mediate all those conflicts out there  with them young guys because the young  guys are looking for help but instead  they're shooting and killing killing one  another because they don't know how they  do not know how to resolve conflicts out  there so it turns deadly t.o uh i've  been to chicago several times  talked with the young brothers talk with  the community try to get the mayor on  the record and one thing that i have  noticed is that these young people  aren't being given a choice anymore the  the violence is ruling the city it's  either you join the gangs or you die now  and so you're not just going after the  the drug dealers and the gang members on  the street you're going after the people  that are responsible for converting  these young minds they don't have a  choice anymore tio  well people have to understand worldwide  the gun violence problem in chicago  baltimore new orleans memphis st louis  is cultural and it's tribal if you do  not address the culturalism with the gun  violence because people are conditioned  to respond a certain way here when it  comes to gun violence so all the experts  out there in the field they do not  understand the culture and the history  of the gun violence with  african-american people and i say this  because over 80 percent of the gun  violence occurs in the african-american  community but today this interview is  about britney so i'm not going to take  up much more time if you don't mind  because i want britney it's all about  brittany benson today yeah i appreciate  that brittany i want to go back to you  um if you had the opportunity to talk to  the mayor  the d.a and all the elected officials  that are representing chicago what would  you tell them  what i would tell them is they need to  do better i don't have no problem with  mayor lightfoot i think she's a nice  person i don't know her personally but  i feel like she could do better but it's  like how could she do better when all  this stuff is  going on in the communities  yeah  so often tio  it is being said that kim fox the d.a is  allowing these offenders to be back out  no bail  they put an ankle bracelet on them and  they commit the crimes again  what would you say to her  well that's what happens when you make  decisions from the mountaintop and  you're not interviewing and talking to  the people down in the valley a lot of  people have been released from prison  well put on put it like this they've  been released from the county jail on  electronic monitoring some of the guys  have uh repeat offenders gun offenders  so when you when they are released they  go out and shoot and kill somebody while  they're while they're out on bond or  electronic monitoring that's not right  so kim fox should stop making decisions  from the mountaintop come down in the  valley and talk to the victims of crime  like brittany benson lost her 15 year  old son and right now in chicago over  100 young people under 15 years old have  been  shot in chicago and so far to date over  460 people have been killed in chicago  over 2 600 people shot to date it makes  no sense that's what's going on in  chicago we need a total new uh strategy  to be implemented here in chicago right  now well i tell you brother i appreciate  the work that you do miss benson i want  you to know that you're loved and i as  long as i'm at fox news i will continue  to cover these stories i will continue  to show up in chicago and highlight this  because it matters to me that could have  been me that could have been someone  that i love in chicago and it has a stop  and i know a lot of people watching this  show feel the same way thank you all so  much for coming on the program tonight  appreciate you hey sean hannity here hey  click here to subscribe to fox news  youtube page and catch our hottest  interviews and most compelling analysis  you will not get it anywhere else

